# The Visitor Design Pattern in Java: A Complete Guide

## Introduction

The **Visitor Design Pattern** is one of the most powerful — and most misunderstood — behavioral design patterns in the Gang of Four (GoF) catalog. It lets you add new operations to a family of related classes **without modifying those classes**. Instead of objects doing every piece of work themselves, they simply "accept" a visitor, and the visitor does the work.

Whether you're preparing for a Java interview, working with Abstract Syntax Trees (ASTs), or designing a large e-commerce system, understanding the Visitor pattern will significantly improve your software design skills.

