## Real-World Example: Document Processing

Let's look at a more practical example — a document processing system that handles different types of documents.

```java
// Element interface
public interface Document {
    void accept(DocumentVisitor visitor);
}

// Concrete Elements
public class PDFDocument implements Document {
    private String fileName;
    private int pages;

    public PDFDocument(String fileName, int pages) {
        this.fileName = fileName;
        this.pages = pages;
    }

    public String getFileName() { return fileName; }
    public int getPages() { return pages; }

    @Override
    public void accept(DocumentVisitor visitor) {
        visitor.visit(this);
    }
}

public class WordDocument implements Document {
    private String fileName;
    private int wordCount;

    public WordDocument(String fileName, int wordCount) {
        this.fileName = fileName;
        this.wordCount = wordCount;
    }

    public String getFileName() { return fileName; }
    public int getWordCount() { return wordCount; }

    @Override
    public void accept(DocumentVisitor visitor) {
        visitor.visit(this);
    }
}

public class SpreadsheetDocument implements Document {
    private String fileName;
    private int rowCount;

    public SpreadsheetDocument(String fileName, int rowCount) {
        this.fileName = fileName;
        this.rowCount = rowCount;
    }

    public String getFileName() { return fileName; }
    public int getRowCount() { return rowCount; }

    @Override
    public void accept(DocumentVisitor visitor) {
        visitor.visit(this);
    }
}

// Visitor interface
public interface DocumentVisitor {
    void visit(PDFDocument pdf);
    void visit(WordDocument word);
    void visit(SpreadsheetDocument spreadsheet);
}

// Concrete Visitor: Text Extraction
public class TextExtractor implements DocumentVisitor {
    private StringBuilder extractedText = new StringBuilder();

    @Override
    public void visit(PDFDocument pdf) {
        extractedText.append("Extracting text from PDF: ")
                     .append(pdf.getFileName())
                     .append(" (").append(pdf.getPages()).append(" pages)\n");
    }

    @Override
    public void visit(WordDocument word) {
        extractedText.append("Extracting text from Word: ")
                     .append(word.getFileName())
                     .append(" (").append(word.getWordCount()).append(" words)\n");
    }

    @Override
    public void visit(SpreadsheetDocument spreadsheet) {
        extractedText.append("Extracting text from Spreadsheet: ")
                     .append(spreadsheet.getFileName())
                     .append(" (").append(spreadsheet.getRowCount()).append(" rows)\n");
    }

    public String getExtractedText() {
        return extractedText.toString();
    }
}

// Concrete Visitor: Document Statistics
public class DocumentStatistics implements DocumentVisitor {
    private int totalPages = 0;
    private int totalWords = 0;
    private int totalRows = 0;

    @Override
    public void visit(PDFDocument pdf) {
        totalPages += pdf.getPages();
    }

    @Override
    public void visit(WordDocument word) {
        totalWords += word.getWordCount();
    }

    @Override
    public void visit(SpreadsheetDocument spreadsheet) {
        totalRows += spreadsheet.getRowCount();
    }

    public void printStatistics() {
        System.out.println("=== Document Statistics ===");
        System.out.println("Total PDF pages: " + totalPages);
        System.out.println("Total Word count: " + totalWords);
        System.out.println("Total Spreadsheet rows: " + totalRows);
    }
}

// Usage
public class DocumentProcessor {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<Document> documents = List.of(
            new PDFDocument("report.pdf", 25),
            new WordDocument("contract.docx", 1500),
            new SpreadsheetDocument("data.xlsx", 500),
            new PDFDocument("manual.pdf", 100)
        );

        TextExtractor extractor = new TextExtractor();
        DocumentStatistics statistics = new DocumentStatistics();

        for (Document doc : documents) {
            doc.accept(extractor);
            doc.accept(statistics);
        }

        System.out.println(extractor.getExtractedText());
        statistics.printStatistics();
    }
}
```

This example demonstrates the true power of the Visitor pattern — we can add new operations (like `CompressDocuments`, `EncryptDocuments`, or `BackupDocuments`) without modifying any of the document classes.

