## Common Pitfalls and Best Practices

### ⚠️ Pitfall 1: Forgetting Double Dispatch
Never call `visitor.visit(shape)` directly. Always use `shape.accept(visitor)`. The direct call uses compile-time type resolution and won't dispatch correctly.

### ⚠️ Pitfall 2: Mutable Visitors in Concurrent Environments
Visitors that accumulate state are not thread-safe. Use separate visitor instances per thread or synchronize access.

### ⚠️ Pitfall
